   "text": "The SMILES below was read region by region from the drawing.\n\n- **Top fragment:** a pyrazine carrying a piperidin-1-yl group, a primary carboxamide and an NH-aryl group. The aryl is a para-substituted phenyl attached to C4 of a piperidine.\n- **Central linker:** the piperidine nitrogen is bonded to a CH2 that leads to a CH. That CH carries a CH2NH group, which is attached to the 4-position of the thalidomide-type isoindoline-1,3-dione bearing the 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group. The same CH is also bonded to C6 of a 2-azaspiro[3.3]heptane.\n- **Azaspiro nitrogen:** it carries a CH2 that leads to a cyclohexane.\n- **Cyclohexane:** it is 1,4-disubstituted, with a wedge bond to the pyrazole nitrogen at one carbon and a hashed bond to the CH2 at the other. A wedge and a hash on opposite ends of the ring mean trans, which I wrote as `[C@H]\u2026[C@H]`. I set the @/@ pairing from my recollection of trans-4-methylcyclohexanol, which I did not re-derive.\n- **Pyrazole:** it is N1-linked to the cyclohexane, has a CHF2 group at C3 and an NH-amide at C4.\n- **Amide partner:** a pyrazolo[1,5-a]pyrimidine-3-carboxamide with a morpholine on the pyrimidine ring.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)c1ncc(N2CCCCC2)nc1Nc1ccc(cc1)C1CCN(CC1)CC(CNc1cccc2c1C(=O)N(C1CCC(=O)NC1=O)C2=O)C1CC2(C1)CN(C2)C[C@H]1CC[C@H](CC1)n1cc(NC(=O)c2cnn3ccc(N4CCOCC4)nc23)c(C(F)F)n1"
